%chk=probe_ch2_uhf.chk
%mem=2GB
%nprocshared=1
#P UHF/6-31G NoSymm Int=NoBasisTransform SCF=(Conver=10)
# Output=(MatrixElement,MO2ElectronIntegrals) Tran=(Full,Force) Window=(2,13)

probe_ch2_uhf: CH2 triplet UHF/6-31G, same geometry and window as the ROHF
probe. UHF is deliberately OUT OF SCOPE for this project -- a spin-restricted
FCIDUMP assumes one set of spatial orbitals, and UHF has two. THE POINT OF THIS
JOB is to find out whether that is detectable from the .mat alone: does it carry
a BETA MO COEFFICIENTS block that the restricted jobs do not? If so, the reader
can refuse UHF input outright instead of silently using the alpha orbitals and
returning a plausible wrong answer. Run it last; it is the cheapest of the set.

0 3
C   0.0000000   0.0000000   0.1900000
H   0.0000000   0.9900000  -0.5600000
H   0.0000000  -0.9900000  -0.5600000

probe_ch2_uhf.mat

